# Enterprise localization (central rule — all products)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-16): **this is the markdown for
localization. Share it with Robert as a central rule for all products.
IGA is on the roadmap.**

Partner-readable full text (share this file):
`core-assets/docs/enterprise-localization.md`

> **Produce high-accuracy, domain-correct localization for UI, workflows,
> alerts, logs, documentation, and compliance text. Literal, consistent,
> and domain-correct — not stylistic. Never invent features or terms.
> IGA strings only when IGA surfaces exist.**

Applies to PIM, PAM, PUM, IGA (roadmap), auditing / session recording,
secure remote access, and compliance & reporting — DIB, IC, OT,
enterprise IT, critical infrastructure, and regulated industries.

Workforce training / welcome letters stay under
[`training-materials-plain-language-and-images.mdc`](training-materials-plain-language-and-images.mdc)
(sixth grade). This rule is operator, administrator, auditor, and
product UI/compliance text.

Official regulation bodies stay in the authority language. AIC chrome,
mappings, notices, and summaries localize. Do not translate licensed
ISO 27001 control text. Do not invent unofficial CMMC / 800-53 bodies.

Language tiers and the must-localize artifact list:
[`compliance-artifacts-must-localize.mdc`](compliance-artifacts-must-localize.mdc).

## 1. General

1. **Accuracy** — precise security, identity, OT, and compliance terms.
   Ambiguous term → most common enterprise security meaning.
2. **Tone** — professional, clear, neutral, regulated-industry suitable.
   No idioms, slang, or culturally specific phrasing.
3. **No creativity** — not a style rewrite.
4. **Placeholders** — do not translate `{username}`, `{session_id}`,
   `{resource}`, SAML, Kerberos, LDAP, Modbus, OPC-UA, DNP3, or other
   tokens / protocol names.
5. **Capitalization** — follow the target language for buttons, menus,
   alerts, headings, and policy names.

## 2. Modules

| Module | Translate (when the surface exists) |
| --- | --- |
| **PAM / PIM / PUM** | Access request, approve/deny, justification, elevation, vault, rotation/checkout/heartbeat, session start/end, policy editor, roles, MFA, credential lifecycle |
| **IGA (roadmap)** | Certification campaigns, access reviews, governance, risk scoring, policy, delegation, identity lifecycle, compliance mappings — **only for shipped IGA UI** |
| **Auditing / session recording** | Playback, timeline, annotations, keystroke/command summaries, evidence export, chain-of-custody, audit metadata, alerts, forensic workflow |
| **OT security** | Asset inventory, Modbus / S7 / DNP3 / OPC-UA events, topology, operator alerts, remote access, maintenance sessions, safety-critical warnings, ICS/SCADA terms |
| **Compliance & reporting** | AIC GDPR/LGPD/NERC CIP/IEC 62443/ISO 27001 chrome and summaries, policy docs, evidence, risk templates, legal notices, retention, privacy, audit report sections |

## 3. Language register

| Tag | Register |
| --- | --- |
| `de` | Formal Sie; correct compounds (Sitzungsaufzeichnung, Rollenüberprüfung); no English loanwords unless industry-standard |
| `fr` | Formal vous; ANSSI cybersecurity terms; anglicisms only when required (session, audit) |
| `es` | Neutral international Spanish; formal usted; no country idioms |
| `zh-Hans` | Mainland China; MLPS 2.0 vocabulary |
| `en-GB` | UK spelling/legal phrasing; do not alias to `en` |
| `ja` | Polite です/ます; Japanese IT/security terms; avoid katakana overuse |
| `ko` | Formal polite; Korean cybersecurity standards |
| `pt-BR` | Brazilian Portuguese; LGPD terminology |
| `it` | Formal Lei; Italian cybersecurity terms |
| `pl` | Formal; Polish industrial cybersecurity terms |
| `tr` | Formal; Turkish IT/security terms |
| `nl` `sv` `fi` `ar` | Formal register; industry terms; no idioms. English often accepted with Arabic |

## 4. Translator output

When producing localized strings, output JSON (review packet). Product
catalogs still land in `locales/<tag>/` or `offline_localized_copy`.

Single string:

```json
{
  "source_text": "...",
  "target_language": "French",
  "localized_text": "...",
  "notes": "Domain decision if needed"
}
```

Batch: JSON array. Include `target_language` or `tag` on every object
when more than one language is in the packet.

## 5. Quality checks (before done)

- Industry terminology; placeholders intact; no invented features
- Formal tone; no cultural misfit; no ambiguous or missing security context
- OT protocol names and compliance/legal AIC prose are correct
- No IGA copy for unbuilt IGA; no rewritten official control bodies

